WEBVTT

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.220
Are you counting money again?

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.360
I gotta. We need to live 
on this for two weeks.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.120
Money certainly is important. 
But you know, Yuichi...

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.830
There is something more important 
than money in the world—

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.580
your friends.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.040
What do you mean by "friends," ma'am?

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.460
Hey! I'm your mother now.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.880
Come on, come on.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.250
M-Mother...

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.930
General Hospital

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.260
How's she doing?

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.580
Oh, Sensei.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:52.690
Yuichi-kun, do you know what the most 
important thing in the world is?

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.110
Yeah, I know.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.120
It's money, right?

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:00.870
Yuichi!

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.700
Are you okay, Yuichi?

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.190
T-Tenji?

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.150
Friendship

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.310
thief

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.310
parent and child crooks

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:41.550
Where are we?

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:39.590
<b>Episode 7: I'll Take 20 Million Yen Worth of Your Life</b>

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.800
<b>Episode 7: I'll Take 20 Million Yen Worth of Your Life</b>

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.670
I don't know.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.270
<i>Hey, guys! Good morning!</i>

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.100
Is that Manabu?

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.530
<i>To prepare for the start of the third game,</i>

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.940
<i>you both have to stay 
in this cave for three days.</i>

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:01.450
<i>So have fun for the next 72 hours, you two!</i>

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.440
Water?

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.810
Only this much for three days?

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.240
Yuichi.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.580
What?

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.460
Well... about what just happened,

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.590
I only did it so I could follow you.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.400
I thought that, with you,

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.890
I could talk about why I betrayed 
everyone and explain everything.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.890
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.260
You know, Yuichi,

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.770
this is my second Tomodachi Game.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.270
S-Second? What is going on?

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.700
It's all Shiho-chan... 
Sawaragi Shiho's fault.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.240
Sawaragi?

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.830
She stole from me... She stole...

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.830
the most precious thing I had in this world.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.590
It began in junior high.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.030
Back then, I had two 
very close best friends.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:03.760
Mikasa Tenji

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.100
Do you want to go into business together?

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.510
I've saved up a million yen.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.460
We can use this and raise more,

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.550
so I can start a business before I'm 18.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.490
That does sound like a great idea, but...

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:18.110
Are you sure you wanna share 
all this money with us?

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:22.530
Don't be stupid. You're the 
only ones I'd do this with.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.780
We had the strongest friendship on campus.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.160
As long as we were together, 
nothing could stop us.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.290
Or so we thought.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.300
Tenji-san, good morning!

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.750
Shiho-chan?

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.080
Oh, that's right, you're in junior high now.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.350
H-Hey, Tenji, who's that girl?

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:45.630
Sawaragi Shiho-san. She's—Well, we've
 been friends since we were kids.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:46.840
Nice to meet you!

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.830
Oh...

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.190
Nice to meet you.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:53.950
After that day, we began to have trouble
 managing our funds, for some reason.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.770
Hey, Tenji.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.920
Are you dating Sawaragi-san?

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:58.560
Huh?

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.710
What are you talking about? 
Right now, our investments need—

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.740
No, this is more important.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.900
W-Well, our parents are trying 
to arrange our marriage,

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.260
but we don't want that. 
We aren't dating.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:11.080
<i>I'd had my suspicions for a while,</i>

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.080
Is that the truth?

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.230
Can we trust you?

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.370
<i>but it seems like they 
both liked Shiho-chan.</i>

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.370
Of course you can.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:22.250
<b>Regular Savings</b>

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:22.250
<b></b>Date<b> | Transaction | Payment Amount | Deposit Amount | Balance | Number</b>

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.520
We were able to start managing 
our funds together again,

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.250
and we still had that money when
 we entered high school together.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.530
Hey, wanna play a game?

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:27.250
We could split the three million 
yen we have now three ways

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:29.150
and invest it separately.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:33.550
Once the total reaches 20 million, 
whoever made the most profit

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.930
gets to be the CEO of our new company.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:38.190
Yeah, that could be interesting.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.760
He'll also get the right 
to propose to Sawaragi!

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.960
Sounds good! I'm all for it!

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:48.180
I honestly had no idea what he was thinking,

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:53.660
but I didn't want to ruin our friendship, 
so I played it off as a joke.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.670
That was the day we were kidnapped, 
taken to the Tomodachi Game site,

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:05.050
and learned the truth that one of us 
was 10 million yen in debt.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.170
Too bad! It's game over in 
the third game for Group B.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.490
Tenji-kun is confirmed as the sole loser.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:15.350
You get everyone's combined debt 
of 20 million yen all to yourself.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:21.390
Since you're still a minor, I'll take
 20 million yen worth of your life.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:24.650
Mahjong - Beginners Welcome

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:25.800
Apple Osteopathic Clinic

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:26.570
Two days later, I was set free

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:29.860
<b>Alcohol 
</b>Cigarettes

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:29.860
under the condition that I would 
never tell anyone what happened.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.250
Hey! Why'd you betray us?!

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.790
Where the hell is our money?!

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:37.700
I-I used all of it for S-Sawaragi-san.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.670
For Shiho-chan?

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:46.630
Gimme a break, Tenji! If I say any
 more, they'll erase me, too!

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.220
Tenji-san, wanna walk home together?

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.510
You seem down these days, Tenji-san.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.890
Is it because your friends transferred?

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.190
Hey, Tenji-san, have you seen them recently?

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:01.020
No.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:05.060
You sure? Someone said they saw 
you talking to one of them.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:06.860
I d-don't think so...

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.860
Hey. What did you talk about?

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:14.780
Like, did you talk about me?

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:22.390
I broke my promise to the 
management and spilled everything

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.750
to the most precious thing...

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.920
the most important <i>person </i>
to me in the world.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.740
What's up, Tenji?

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.830
My father, who raised me on his own.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:41.270
Fun <b>Vehicle 
Picture Book</b>

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:40.670
For me, he was like a living textbook.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.520
I'm really glad you told me, Tenji.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:45.610
Dad...

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.500
I'm sure it was hard 
keeping that to yourself.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.940
Let me take care of everything from here.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:02.000
Uncle! Why... Why is Dad...

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:07.640
We don't know the details yet, 
but it's safe to say it was a suicide.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.830
<i>A suicide? That can't be right. 
My dad was...</i>

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:15.140
Tenji, this might be a big deal.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:19.080
I'm going to Sawaragi's house to
 ask Shiho-chan about it directly.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.220
B-But...

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.780
Hey, don't worry.

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:23.440
If anything happens, Wataru will be there.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:27.740
He's my best friend in the world. 
I know he'll have my back.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.670
I couldn't trust anyone.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:35.580
But Sawaragi Shiho was clearly at the center

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.110
of everything that was happening.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:43.850
After that, I decided to investigate
 Shiho-chan thoroughly.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.990
But that didn't go well, either.

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.250
What do you mean?

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.590
I got an email from an unknown sender.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:56.840
Quit sticking your nose into 
Sawaragi Shiho's business. 
If you don't, you'll disappear too. 
Just like Mikasa Yutaka.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:56.840
So I decided to gamble. 
It was all or nothing.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.370
I'd play the Tomodachi Game

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:01.850
to corner her and make her 
show her true colors.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.390
And that's the real reason you applied?

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:06.270
That's right.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:10.610
But then I screwed up your plan, huh?

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.150
No, not really.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:16.280
Shiho-chan told one really big lie.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.280
A lie?

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.280
Yeah. And once you hear about it,

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.580
you should believe that Sawaragi Shiho 
was the real traitor, too.

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:33.170
The key is the fact that our total combined
 debt right now is 10.8 million yen.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:33.170
Shibe Makoto

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:33.170
Sawaragi Shiho

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:33.170
Kokorogi Yutori

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:33.170
Mikasa Tenji

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:33.170
Katagiri Yuichi

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.400
10.8 million?

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.260
That doesn't add up.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.180
Yeah. To be exact—

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:43.060
Wait a second! How would you 
know the total debt amount?

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.680
It's the same as when I played before.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:50.230
Once you clear the second game, 
the management will tell you the total debt.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:54.110
Manabu-kun! Tell us the total 
debt amount again.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.510
<i>Fine, whatever.</i>

00:09:56.510 --> 00:10:02.490
<i>The current total debt amount 
for Group C is 10.8 million yen.</i>

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:05.000
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:10.250
If we take everyone 
at their word, it looks like this.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:16.590
<b>Yuichi -4.1 million yen

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.520
That's 8 million off from 10.8 million yen.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:16.590
Which means someone's
 lying about their debt.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.590
Yeah, it does...

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:22.800
By the way, I also told a lie 
at the end of the first game.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:27.810
If the 10 yen coin goes to "yes," you clear the game. 
If the 10 yen coin goes to "no," only the reader's debt will be halved.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:27.810
My question card actually said 
I could cut my debt in half.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:32.260
So at the end of the first game, 
I was at minus 1.6 million yen,

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:36.820
and my real debt right now 
is 2.1 million yen.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.820
<b>Tenji    -2.1 million yen</b>

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:41.200
Then it's likely Shibe got the same thing.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.200
<b><u><u>Shibe Makoto </u>
Debt: 3.6 million yen
 (self-reported)</u></b>

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:45.700
Shibe's current debt amount 
is probably 200,000 yen.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.700
<b>Shibe    -200,000 yen</b>

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.440
<b>Yuichi -4.1 million yen

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:49.590
But even if we correct 
both of your amounts...

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.820
<b>Yuichi -4.1 million yen

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:52.080
<b>Yuichi -4.1 million yen 

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:52.080
We're still off by 4 million.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>Shibe</b>

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>Yutori</b>

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>Shiho     -6.2 million yen</b>

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:56.460
<b>Total -14.8 million yen</b>

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:56.790
Right. Sawaragi's 6.2 million 
debt is too high.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:11:02.480
If we assume she didn't get a penalty, 
she'd have 2.2 million yen in debt.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.180
<b><u>Sawaragi Shiho</u> 
Debt: 3.6 million yen 
(self-reported)</b>

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.090
<b>Shiho    -2.2 million yen</b>

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.080
<b>Yuichi -4.1 million yen 

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:03.890
You're right.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:04.210
<b>Yuichi -4.1 million yen 

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.970
<b>Yuichi -4.1 million yen 

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.970
That way, everything adds up.

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:11.600
I feel bad, but I eavesdropped on you two.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:16.770
Yuichi, what if everything 
she said was a lie?

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:20.900
What would you think of
 Sawaragi Shiho then?

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:27.370
That she's quite the scam artist.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:32.370
Yeah. Can you imagine how dark 
she really is, deep inside?

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.180
If you're telling the truth, that is.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:37.090
<b>Actually, Sawaragi Shiho 
has had plastic surgery.</b>

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:40.680
The only thing any of us can be
 sure about is our own debt.

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:37.550
<b>Bad-Mouth</b>

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:37.550
<b></b>Actually, Sawaragi Shiho 
has had plastic surgery.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:44.890
No matter how convincing it sounds, 
I can't trust anything one hundred percent.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.100
You must have realized by now.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:52.730
We thought we knew each other, 
but we're basically strangers.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.390
You didn't know what kind of person I was,

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.570
like that I was a killer, right?

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:03.320
But you still followed me. Why?

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.450
That's...

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:11.060
because you said you were going to 
destroy the Tomodachi Game.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:15.340
I have only one goal: to avenge 
my father's death.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:19.420
And the key to that is the Sawaragi family 
and this Tomodachi Game.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.720
Yuichi, I want you to fight with me.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:24.890
Do you really mean that?

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:29.180
I think you're probably 
a really dangerous person.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:33.190
I saw the face of true evil in you.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:35.650
But you do have strength, right?

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:38.910
The strength to truly destroy 
the management?

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.610
We can't fight fair.

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:43.780
We won't be able to beat them 
unless we take some risks!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:49.050
No way. Like I just said,
 talk like that is meaningless now.

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:50.160
You're right.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.100
Mikasa Tenji

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.290
My debt right now is 2.1 million.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.920
Yuichi, trust me!

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.460
Idiot! Stop it!

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:03.470
Fine, I won't ask you 
to join my fight anymore.

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:09.010
But at least let me follow you on yours.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:13.350
I swear I won't get in your way! 
I don't care if you use me like a tool!

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:16.270
So Yuichi, I beg you...

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:20.730
You're... You're my last and only hope!

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.880
We have three days.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.420
Let me think it over in that time.

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:32.180
Now get up and stop begging. Please.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:39.710
<b>About 60 hours later</b>

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:40.010
Hey, Tenji. What do "friends" mean to you?

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:41.480
I have no idea.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:45.380
I stopped thinking about it 
after my best friends betrayed me.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.600
So regardless of Sawaragi,

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:50.630
Kokorogi and Shibe are just people 
you met while planning your revenge.

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:51.840
Like strangers?

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.680
I guess so.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:57.310
I don't believe you.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.230
If they were nothing but strangers,

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.170
why did you pick them 
for the Tomodachi Game?

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:06.410
You must have thought they 
had some feelings for you.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:11.300
Those two had no idea they were being used

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:13.660
and thought I was their friend.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:18.160
They're just... real idiots.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.360
Tenji, promise me one thing.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:24.340
Hmm?

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:27.380
When we get back, apologize to them.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:31.440
Even if I did, there's no way 
they'd forgive me.

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:33.310
It doesn't matter. Apologize anyway.

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:38.270
If there's at least some part
 of you that feels guilt, do it.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:40.810
Okay.

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:49.400
All right. If you're going to keep 
that promise, I'll make one, too.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:55.540
I'm going to clear this third game, 
no matter what it takes.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:15:00.120
<b>72 hours later...</b>

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:02.540
<i>Three days are up! Come on outside.</i>

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:07.680
Let's go, Tenji. We have to 
make it back to everyone.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:08.680
Yeah.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.010
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.220
Ah, you've both come out.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:22.140
Manabu-kun... is that you?

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:24.440
Fool! Who are you calling Manabu-kun?!

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:36.200
I'm the one and only Sergeant Manabu!

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:40.420
The third game is starting.

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:43.080
Yes. It looks like they're up 
against your group.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.920
That's right!

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:48.880
And how's your Group C?

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:51.680
Huh? There are only two left?

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:54.730
The game's over before it even started.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.180
I wonder about that.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:02.780
Huh? In the third game, the bigger team
 always has the advantage.

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:03.830
Wanna bet?

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:05.940
I'm in.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:09.180
All right, let's get started, you pigs!

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.010
The third game...

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:14.660
Friendly Hide-and-Seek!

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.910
Just two? That's brutal.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.160
And both dudes, too. What a waste.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.670
It's rude to call them a waste, Senpai.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:28.170
Your battle power is a mere five, 
huh? Piece of trash!

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:30.920
Huh?! You wanna piece of dis?

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:32.970
Who the hell are they?

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.220
Let me say, first of all, 
that this game is held in...

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.510
<b>Competitive Battle Format</b>

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:38.510
competitive battle format!

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:41.270
The winners will clear the third game.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.730
For the losers, it's game over.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.940
Wait a minute!

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:48.110
Isn't the Tomodachi Game supposed 
to test friendships within the group?

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.110
Mm-hmm.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.820
It will test your true friendship
 precisely <i>because</i> you have opponents.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:56.330
For instance, what if 
your teammate is a jerk

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:58.740
who betrayed everyone by bad-mouthing them...

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:04.750
But the opposing team has five friends 
who all cooperated with each other?

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:07.540
Then the grass looks 
greener on the other side.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:09.460
Wait, it actually <i>is</i> greener!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.630
You'll start comparing yourselves 
to them, you'll get jealous,

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:16.340
and then, how do you think it'll all end?

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:18.320
It... It'll...

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:21.730
Trusting your friends will start 
to look like a dumb idea.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:22.770
Yuichi?

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.800
Correct! This game will make you 
battle against that kind of feeling.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:29.320
No matter how hard it is, 
you have to trust your friends,

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.970
and then you wait, and wait, 
and wait, and wait, and wait,

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:34.240
<b></b>wait and wait and wait and wait

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:33.370
and wait, and keep waiting...

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:37.380
That's the game! 
That's Friendly Hide-and-Seek!

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.740
<b></b>Friendly Hide-and-Seek

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:45.450
From here on, you will all play 
hide-and-seek in this huge forest.

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:50.260
Each team will choose one hider 
who will hide somewhere in the forest.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:53.130
<b>Hider</b>

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:53.130
<b>Hider</b>

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:53.130
<b>Seeker</b>

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:53.130
<b>Seeker</b>

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:52.340
The remaining team members 
will be the seekers.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:56.760
I see. That's why you said the 
third game can't be cleared alone.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:58.130
<b>Ugh...</b>

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:58.130
<b></b>Seeker

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:58.130
<b></b>Hider

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.130
That's right.

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:02.140
And the team that finds 
the other's hider first wins.

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:02.140
<b></b>Hider

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:02.140
<b><b>I found Manabu-kun!</b></b>

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:02.140
<b></b>Seeker

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:03.330
Wait a minute.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:07.520
With two people, we have only 
one seeker. That's totally...

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:11.440
Right! In this game, the smaller team 
is at a huge disadvantage.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:14.360
But that's just the way it goes.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:16.770
This is the Tomodachi Game.

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:19.080
Your team had a huge argument.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:22.240
Obviously, a team that gets along 
will have an advantage.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:27.120
I'll explain again later, 
but here are the rules.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b>Third Game Rules</b>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b><b>Can't Do</b></b>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b><b>Be Violent</b></b>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b><b>Move the Hider</b></b>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b><b>Can Do</b></b>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b><b>Contact</b></b>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b><b>Eat</b></b>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b><b>Surrender (Give Up)</b></b>

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.370
<b><b>Change Sides (Switch)</b></b>

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:29.370
Take a close look.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.780
<b><b>Change Sides </b>(Switch)</b>

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.240
What's this "change sides" one?

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.170
If it looks like your team is about to lose,

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:41.720
the seekers can switch sides 
to the enemy team.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:46.090
But even if the team you switch to wins, 
you won't go on to the fourth game.

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:49.460
Is there any point to switching, then?

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:55.730
Of course there is.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:58.400
If you're on the winning team 
when the game ends,

00:18:55.730 --> 00:19:01.610
<b>Winning Team</b>

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:02.870
<b>-1 million yen</b>

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:01.250
the personal debt that you would 
have gained from failing to clear

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:04.680
can all be passed to the losing team.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:05.240
<b>Losing Team</b>

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.240
<b>-250,000 yen  -250,000 yen  -250,000 yen  -250,000 yen</b>

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.240
<b>0 yen</b>

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:08.070
So even if they fail to clear, 
the person who switched

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:10.710
can end the game with no debt.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:16.170
<b>Money</b>

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:16.170
<b>Friends</b>

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:13.940
<i>Do you choose friends or money?</i>

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.170
<i>That's what the Tomodachi Game
 is really about.</i>

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:18.520
In particular, when 
there's only two on a team,

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:21.430
if one person switches, 
the game immediately ends.

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.550
So be careful!

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:26.810
Don't worry. I have no 
intention of switching.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:28.730
I really hope not. That would suck.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.560
But even on a five-person team...

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:36.150
It's possible for four to switch, 
leaving all of their debt on the one hider.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.980
So that is an option.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:41.860
What happens if you switch but still lose?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:45.870
In that case, the traitor will 
receive an amount of debt

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:47.860
equal to the average debt 
of the losing team.

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:51.330
They then return to their original team, 
and continue to the fourth game.

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:55.840
If someone betrays their team but
 then returns with even more debt...

00:19:56.530 --> 00:19:58.250
That'd be unforgivable, huh?

00:19:58.250 --> 00:19:58.880
Ah!

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:04.860
And just so you know, trading 
name tags is prohibited this time.

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:09.320
All right! Now all we have to do 
is choose the hiders.

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:13.690
But first, I have some exclusive 
information for the two in Group C!

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:18.430
There's a player from another group 
who made it to the third game alone.

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:20.850
Do you want to add them to your team?

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:24.200
Only if you say it's okay, of course.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.670
W-Why would we ever accept—

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:27.810
Are they a girl?

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:30.490
Huh? Yeah, she's a cute girl.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:31.570
In that case, it's okay.

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:35.120
Huh? What? Really? It's okay if it's a girl?

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:35.120
Yuichi! It's too dangerous 
to let an outsider in!

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:36.800
You're such a perv, Yuichi-kun!

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:37.350
If she betrays us, we're finished!

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.690
I know.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:42.950
But it would be almost impossible 
for the two of us to win.

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:45.480
You're sure? Are you sure, then?

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:47.720
You guys are such a pain. I'll get her.

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:49.670
Please come over!

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:56.100
All right, please introduce yourself!

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.980
I'm Mizuse Maria.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:00.320
Wow!

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:05.700
<i>That's the guy who said 
he'd destroy the operation?</i>

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:08.320
When the higher-ups were alerted,

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:10.900
they decided to send Maria
 in to keep an eye on him.

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:13.710
I was wondering what he'd be like,

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:18.210
but if he let her in that easily, 
he can't be that deep.

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:22.330
Besides trusting your friends,

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:24.720
there is one other way 
to clear the Tomodachi Game.

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:26.720
Do you know what that is?

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:28.330
It's...

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:32.510
To lead your group 
with overwhelming charisma!

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:33.890
And...

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:38.350
My Group K has that charisma. 
In fact, it has a genius.

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:43.750
I'm sure you'll figure out which one 
the genius is eventually.

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:46.510
I wonder about that.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:52.410
I doubt very much that even 
a genius could kill a monster.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:54.450
Listen up.

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:59.170
I'm gonna hide, and you don't 
have a snowball's chance in hell,

00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:02.750
because I'll never give up. 
Even if it kills me.

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:07.090
Yuichi.

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:09.420
I'll be the hider.

00:22:09.420 --> 00:22:10.220
Are you sure?

00:22:10.220 --> 00:22:14.920
It's got to be me. 
I can't make you sit still.

00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:19.580
And I hate to say it, but we can't 
give her the option to give up.

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:22.610
You're right. Sorry, man.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:24.610
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:29.740
It seems both teams 
have chosen their hider.

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:32.330
I'll give you two hours 
to find your hiding spots.

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:36.980
First, proceed in opposite 
directions, west or east.

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:40.500
All right. Third game, start!

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:45.960
<b>Third Game</b>

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:45.960
<b>Friendly Hide-and-Seek</b>

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:45.960
<b>Start</b>

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:49.970
<b>NEXT: It's a Game Where You Wait, and Wait, and Wait... and Keep Waiting</b>
